  "body": "Goal: Edit a tool in the tool library window, in a Tool tab and a Details tab. Apply is one undo step.\n\nParent: #3663. Plan: the implementation plan in the #3663 comment. This is PR U2 of 11. Refs #898: its fields show on the Details tab.\n\nFiles:\n- Add `tool_library_dialog/rail.rs`. The list folds into a rail when a tool is open.\n- Add `tool_library_dialog/tool_tab.rs`. Make `geometry`, `kind_rows` and `catalog` in `tool_settings_grid.rs` `pub(super)` and call them. Do not copy them. Then #3368 and #3369 add their rows in one place.\n- Add `tool_library_dialog/details_tab.rs`. It uses `tool_catalog_rows::catalog_rows`, the material group and the tool number.\n- Apply calls `State::apply_tool_numbers` and `push_number_if_changed` in `tool_settings.rs`.\n- Add an \"Edit tool shape\" button that calls `actions::open_tool_shape_editor`.\n- The dialog keeps its own draft in `ToolLibraryView`. Properties keeps `state.tool_ui`. Swap the two around the draw and Apply. `sync_tool_ui` must not reset the dialog draft while the user types.\n\nTests (new): `layout_window_tool_editor`, `tool_library_editor::apply_is_one_change_tool_and_undo_restores`, `tool_library_editor::the_dialog_draft_and_the_properties_draft_do_not_mix`, `tool_library_editor::details_tab_shows_the_catalog_facts`.\n\nDepends on: U1 (the U1 issue, #3892).\n\nCommands: `ChangeTool` and the tool-number command. Nothing new. No MCP tool is owed.\n\nExpected quick gate: 10 steps, plus `state` (not measured).\n\nDone means: a user opens a tool in the window, edits geometry and catalog facts, and applies. One undo step restores the old tool. The dialog and Properties drafts do not mix.\n\nChangelog row: Edit a tool's geometry and catalog facts in the tool library window. Apply is one undo step.\n",
